## 7. CDI — DEPENDENCY INJECTION

Quarkus uses **ArC** — a build-time CDI (Contexts and Dependency Injection) implementation.

### Scopes

| Scope | Annotation | Lifecycle | Use Case |
|-------|-----------|-----------|----------|
| Application | `@ApplicationScoped` | One instance for entire app | Services, repositories |
| Request | `@RequestScoped` | One instance per HTTP request | Request-specific data |
| Session | `@SessionScoped` | One instance per session | Web sessions |
| Dependent | `@Dependent` | New instance each injection | Stateless helpers |
| Singleton | `@Singleton` | One instance (eager) | Global state |

### Basic DI Examples
```java
// ---- SERVICE (Bean) ----
import jakarta.enterprise.context.ApplicationScoped;

@ApplicationScoped  // <-- Makes this a CDI bean
public class GreetingService {

    public String greet(String name) {
        return "Hello, " + name + "!";
    }
}

// ---- INJECTION via @Inject ----
import jakarta.inject.Inject;
import jakarta.ws.rs.GET;
import jakarta.ws.rs.Path;

@Path("/greet")
public class GreetingResource {

    @Inject  // <-- Field injection
    GreetingService greetingService;

    @GET
    public String hello() {
        return greetingService.greet("World");
    }
}

// ---- CONSTRUCTOR INJECTION (preferred) ----
@Path("/greet")
public class GreetingResource {

    private final GreetingService greetingService;

    @Inject  // Can be omitted if single constructor
    public GreetingResource(GreetingService greetingService) {
        this.greetingService = greetingService;
    }

    @GET
    public String hello() {
        return greetingService.greet("World");
    }
}
```

### Qualifiers (When Multiple Implementations Exist)
```java
import jakarta.inject.Qualifier;
import java.lang.annotation.*;

@Qualifier
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)
@Target({ElementType.FIELD, ElementType.PARAMETER, ElementType.TYPE})
public @interface Premium {}

// Implementation 1
@ApplicationScoped
public class StandardGreeting implements GreetingService {
    public String greet(String name) { return "Hi " + name; }
}

// Implementation 2
@Premium
@ApplicationScoped
public class PremiumGreeting implements GreetingService {
    public String greet(String name) { return "Welcome, esteemed " + name + "!"; }
}

// Injection
@Inject
@Premium
GreetingService greetingService;  // Gets PremiumGreeting
```

