## 14. REACTIVE PROGRAMMING (MUTINY)

**Mutiny** is Quarkus's reactive programming library. Two main types:
- **`Uni<T>`** — emits 0 or 1 item (like CompletableFuture, Mono)
- **`Multi<T>`** — emits 0 to N items (like Stream, Flux)

### Uni — Single Result
```java
// Create
Uni<String> greeting = Uni.createFrom().item("Hello");
Uni<String> empty = Uni.createFrom().nullItem();
Uni<String> failed = Uni.createFrom().failure(new RuntimeException("Oops"));

// Transform
Uni<String> upper = greeting
    .onItem().transform(s -> s.toUpperCase());  // "HELLO"

// Chain (flatMap)
Uni<Person> person = Uni.createFrom().item(1L)
    .onItem().transformToUni(id -> personService.findById(id));

// Handle errors
Uni<String> safe = greeting
    .onFailure().recoverWithItem("Default Value");

Uni<String> retried = greeting
    .onFailure().retry().atMost(3);

// Combine
Uni<Tuple2<Person, Address>> combined = Uni.combine().all()
    .unis(personUni, addressUni)
    .asTuple();

// Subscribe
greeting.subscribe().with(
    item -> System.out.println("Got: " + item),
    failure -> System.out.println("Failed: " + failure)
);
```

### Multi — Stream of Items
```java
// Create
Multi<Integer> numbers = Multi.createFrom().items(1, 2, 3, 4, 5);
Multi<Integer> range = Multi.createFrom().range(1, 100);
Multi<Long> ticks = Multi.createFrom().ticks().every(Duration.ofSeconds(1));

// Transform
Multi<String> strings = numbers
    .onItem().transform(n -> "Number: " + n);

// Filter
Multi<Integer> evens = numbers
    .select().where(n -> n % 2 == 0);

// Collect
Uni<List<Integer>> list = numbers.collect().asList();
Uni<Map<String, Integer>> map = numbers.collect()
    .asMap(n -> "key-" + n);

// Merge multiple streams
Multi<String> merged = Multi.createBy().merging()
    .streams(stream1, stream2);
```

### Reactive REST Endpoints
```java
@Path("/api/reactive")
public class ReactiveResource {

    @GET
    @Path("/hello")
    public Uni<String> hello() {
        return Uni.createFrom().item("Hello Reactive!");
    }

